"author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLAIM: plan-review gate bypassed by user approval — no plan-review attestation was verified. Reason: \"plan-review PASSED (multiple REVIEW_RESULT sidecars record verdict PASS) but attestation persistence lost the tracker-head race ~20 consecutive times under continuous multi-agent write load (plan_review_generation_retry: head moved every attempt); operator-directed signing-starvation remediation\".","timestamp":1787453576759439001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC3 audit — remaining --json mutation wrappers in acli_cli_ops (and the module-level acli.py wrappers), checked for the raw-passthrough pattern this ticket fixed in add_comment:\n\n- create_issue paths (_create_issue_no_json, _create_from_json_payload): both return the CompletedProcess to _create_issue_from_json, which routes stdout through _verify_created_issue (parses, REST/subprocess-verifies, raises loudly on missing key). NOT raw passthrough. OK.\n- update_priority: REST PUT via urllib, returns None, no ACLI JSON parse. OK.\n- get_issue: unwraps issues[0], raises 'Issue not found' when absent. OK (read).\n- get_comments -> _parse_paginated_comments -> _parse_acli_comments: normalizes bare-list/wrapped-dict/unrecognized shapes. OK (read).\n- add_comment: fixed by this ticket (_parse_comment_created; Gerrit change 2144).\n\nFINDING (latent, same class): module-level acli.update_issue (acli.py, 'workitem edit --json' branch) still returns raw json.loads(result.stdout) — the batch mutation envelope — while its docstring/type suggest an issue resource. Mitigations today: _run_acli's _check_mutation_failure raises AcliMutationError on FAILURE envelopes (bug 44de), and the only production consumer chain (dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update -> update_one -> apply_handlers.handle_update) treats the return opaquely (None-or-dict; no field reads), so no consumer-reachable hazard exists today. Not fixed here to keep this change surgical; flagging for a follow-up if a consumer ever starts reading fields from update_issue's return.","timestamp":1787454654776152001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"EVIDENCE OF COMPLETION — merged.\n\nChange: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2144 (LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, submitted; merged as f403b97e4c on main).\n\nWhat landed: acli_cli_ops.add_comment now returns _parse_comment_created(result.stdout) — a dict WITHOUT envelope markers (results/successCount) passes through verbatim (DC/REST comment resource); the Cloud batch envelope normalizes to {\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <parsed>} so results[].id (a WORK ITEM key) can never be mistaken for a comment id; any other shape raises loudly. _record_comment_id docstring updated to the normalized contract.\n\nACs:\n- AC1 (normalizer, recorded-envelope fixtures): DONE — tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py: ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE + live-recorded ACLI_FAILURE_ENVELOPE (acli 1.3.19-stable, provenance noted in file); success-envelope-normalized, resource-passthrough, unrecognized-raises, failure-envelope-raises-AcliMutationError. 8 passed.\n- AC2 (no consumer sees the raw envelope): DONE — the only production consumer chain (_record_comment_id) exercised via the seam-crossing suite (change 2145).\n- AC3 (audit of other raw --json passthroughs): DONE — recorded in prior comment: acli.update_issue raw passthrough is latent-only (no consumer reads fields).\n\nGates: targeted 30 passed + apply/diffing/mutate suites 963 passed; make lint (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); make typecheck clean. Also fixed the two suite-level guards the new symbol tripped in CI (rate-limit sweep NON-MUTATING classification; timeout-test payload expectation) — in the same change, patchset 2.","timestamp":1787465539808671001}],"created_at":1787254294337250001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a7575743-3e5b-4bb8-9aed-8015529bc030","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615"},{"link_uuid":"2b273cdb-103b-40a9-aa2b-5e7fd92bcc2d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fea5-a325-7f50-43f4"},{"link_uuid":"522c63d1-8a1c-4963-a131-13ba0e84c24b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"654b-a2c4-25d4-4174"},{"link_uuid":"908053f9-bfe0-405b-a589-b58abbabfe8b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b971-b789-63c8-4586"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.add_comment` is the only `--json` consumer in that module that\nreturns raw `json.loads(result.stdout)` straight to its caller\n(`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py:549-550`). Every sibling\nnormalizes or verifies the payload first: `get_comments` -> `_parse_paginated_comments`,\n`_parse_acli_comments` (normalizes bare list / wrapped dict / unrecognised shape), `get_issue`\n(unwraps `issues[0]`, raises when absent), `create_issue` -> `_verify_created_issue` (raises\nloudly when no key, `acli_cli_ops.py:40`).\n\nBecause `add_comment` skips that idiom, it hands its caller ACLI's batch mutation envelope\n(`{\"results\": [...], \"totalCount\": N, \"successCount\": N}`) while its declared type\n(`_backend.py:585`: `add_comment(...) -> dict[str, Any]`) and its consumer\n(`dispatch_apply_phases._record_comment_id`, which reads `result.get(\"id\")`) treat it as a\ncreated comment resource. That gap is exactly what let bug `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker`\n(`aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`) ship: `_record_comment_id` read `result[\"id\"]`, got `None` on every\nCloud post, and silently no-opped — re-posting ~205 comments an hour until REB-1861 hit Jira's\n5000-comment cap. The aa7b fix made `_record_comment_id` tolerant (records\n`UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID` when no id), but the transport boundary itself still returns the\nsemantically-wrong shape, and `results[].id` (the WORK ITEM key) remains a trap for any future\nconsumer.\n\n## Approach\n\nNormalize at the transport boundary, mirroring the sibling idiom:\n\n1. Add a module-level helper `_parse_comment_created(stdout: str) -> dict[str, Any]` in\n   `acli_cli_ops.py`, called by `add_comment` in place of raw `json.loads`:\n   - A dict WITHOUT the batch-envelope markers (`results` / `successCount`) is a comment\n     resource (the DC/REST-shaped `{\"id\": \"10001\"}` that\n     `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py:52` pins) — returned\n     verbatim. Assume any non-envelope dict is a resource (default; no shape allowlist).\n   - The batch envelope is returned as an honest comment-resource-shaped dict\n     `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <parsed>}`: explicit `id: None` because ACLI echoes no\n     comment id, envelope preserved under a clearly-named key so `results[].id` (the WORK\n     ITEM key, not a comment id) can never be mistaken for one. FAILURE envelopes never reach\n     the normalizer: `acli_subprocess._run_acli` already raises `AcliMutationError` via\n     `_check_mutation_failure` (`acli_subprocess.py:299-345`, bug 44de).\n   - Any other shape (bare list, scalar, non-JSON handled by json.loads raising) raises\n     `RuntimeError` naming the payload, mirroring `_verify_created_issue`'s loud failure.\n2. Update the `acli_result` fixture assertions in\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` (which currently pin\n   the raw-envelope passthrough) to the normalized contract; its four dedup tests must keep\n   passing unchanged (the recording path still stores `UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID`).\n3. Commit a RECORDED real ACLI comment-create payload: the failure envelope captured live\n   today against acli 1.3.19 via the safe probe\n   `acli jira workitem comment create --key NONEXIST-999999 --json` (exit=0,\n   `successCount: 0`, `results[0].id == \"NONEXIST-999999\"` — no mutation performed). Embed it\n   as a constant with a provenance note and assert `_check_mutation_failure` raises\n   `AcliMutationError` on it, plus normalizer unit tests against the already-recorded SUCCESS\n   envelope (verified live against acli 1.3.19 by fix 8d98c298fa8).\n4. Audit the remaining `--json` mutation wrappers for raw passthrough —\n   `acli_cli_ops.create_issue` paths (`_create_issue_no_json`, `_create_from_json_payload`),\n   `update_priority` (REST, no JSON return), `get_issue`, `get_comments`, and the\n   module-level `acli.update_issue` (`acli.py:211` returns `json.loads(result.stdout)` raw\n   for `workitem edit`) — and record the findings as a comment on this ticket; file a\n   `discovered_from` ticket for any consumer-reachable hazard found.\n5. Touch up the `_record_comment_id` docstring (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:311`) so its\n   description of the Cloud transport's return matches the normalized shape.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py` — add\n  `_parse_comment_created`; `add_comment` routes through it.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` — update fixture\n  assertions to the normalized contract; add recorded failure-envelope constant + tests.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` — docstring-only update to\n  `_record_comment_id`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: the recorded SUCCESS envelope driven through the real\n  `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` (stubbed at the `_run_acli` seam, as the existing fixture does)\n  returns `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": <envelope>}`; the DC/REST-shaped `{\"id\": \"10001\"}`\n  passes through verbatim (existing `test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py` assertion keeps\n  passing).\n- Failure/edge: the RECORDED failure envelope raises `AcliMutationError` in\n  `_check_mutation_failure`; a bare-list payload makes `_parse_comment_created` raise\n  `RuntimeError`.\n- Regression: all four existing dedup tests in `test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py` pass with\n  the normalized fixture (recording stores `UNKNOWN_COMMENT_ID`; re-diff emits nothing).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `add_comment` no longer returns the raw batch envelope: SUCCESS envelope ->\n      `{\"id\": None, \"acli_envelope\": ...}`, resource-shaped payload -> verbatim, unrecognized\n      shape -> `RuntimeError` — checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py`.\n- [x] At least one test asserts against a RECORDED real ACLI comment-create payload (the\n      live-captured failure envelope with its provenance note) rather than an invented one —\n      checked by reading the committed constant's provenance comment and running its test.\n- [x] The remaining `acli_cli_ops` `--json` mutation wrappers (and `acli.update_issue`) are\n      audited for raw passthrough and the finding is recorded as a comment on this ticket —\n      checked by the comment's presence on the ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py","reason":"add _parse_comment_created normalizer; add_comment routes through it"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_acli_envelope.py","reason":"update fixture assertions to normalized contract; add recorded failure-envelope constant and tests"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py","reason":"docstring-only update to _record_comment_id describing the normalized Cloud return"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","654b-a2c4-25d4-4174"],["relates_to","b971-b789-63c8-4586"],["relates_to","fea5-a325-7f50-43f4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8e083ff9-cf56-41a9-b42e-4871c29f4f7f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3235-8aaf-e288-48f2","ticket_type":"task","title":"ACLI add_comment returns the raw batch envelope, not a comment resource","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["51bca6af-9185-448a-88c4-f818710e987e","c6cbf274-e9e6-4936-bc68-b049d3575104","f52b821c-6b6f-448f-9749-7de2139834ce","9c595edf-52c3-48ae-b7c9-a5d42f6146a8","8e083ff9-cf56-41a9-b42e-4871c29f4f7f","0b430c60-cc38-43f4-8c96-e65d6090f7e6","1809e5f2-46aa-4142-a2ba-f59f931c7019","2b273cdb-103b-40a9-aa2b-5e7fd92bcc2d","522c63d1-8a1c-4963-a131-13ba0e84c24b","908053f9-bfe0-405b-a589-b58abbabfe8b","78aec243-458b-4639-9e2f-0db5ceb6e804","fb444a56-ec3d-4fe3-be73-959b08dc5be5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787465594273805002,"uuid":"da5d5db6-99a2-435c-b20d-c75c57afae96"}